{"ts": 0.199518, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[93menv  5/6\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
{"ts": 0.199573, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.19963, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mA program that reads a variable\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 46}
{"ts": 0.199644, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "This tutor is configured the same way. It reads \u001b[92mSHELLTUTOR_HOME\u001b[0m to\r\ndecide where your practice folder goes.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mecho \"[$SHELLTUTOR_HOME]\"\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# [] means: not set, so the default is used\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[0m                           \u001b[90m# where you are now, inside the practice folder\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nTo put the folder somewhere else, set the variable on the line that\r\nstarts the tutor:   \u001b[92mSHELLTUTOR_HOME=~/practice ./shelltutor\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Run both, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 509}
{"ts": 0.203308, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
